The rejected attempt never created the five new files, so every test failed on imports. This version adds them and keeps the edits to the existing files from last time. I haven't run the tests.

- **Circular import:** the new model and helper import `VoiceBroadcastInfoEventType` and `VoiceBroadcastInfoState` from the `src/voice-broadcast` barrel, which in turn re-exports them. This only works because those values are read when methods run, not when modules load. If anything starts using them at import time, it will break.
- **Waiting for the started event:** in `startNewVoiceBroadcastRecording`, a room-state update can arrive before the send returns an event id. The handler only resolves once the event id is known, there is a state event, and the ids match. The match isn't re-checked straight after the send, so if the room's last update came before the send returned, the promise waits for the next one.
- **Tile title:** it now reads `<userId> • <room name>` as specified, so it shows the sender's user id instead of their display name.

