## Approach

`read_subjects` is rewritten as a per-tag dispatch, with the subdivision mapping in one shared helper. `find_aspects` and `re_aspects` are removed, so aspect detection no longer affects classification or drops subdivision values.

The double-count is fixed in the `610` handler: it builds one `org` entry from the combined `a`, `b`, `c`, `d` values and no longer counts subfield `a` separately. That also keeps the organization name out of `subject`. Subdivisions `v`/`x`/`y`/`z` still map to `subject`/`time`/`place` for every tag, `610` included.

The `pyproject.toml` per-file ignore for `get_subjects.py` is removed, since the function no longer needs the complexity suppressions. I have not run the tests.

## Behaviour changes to be aware of

- The `651` and `z` place handlers now skip whitespace-only values before calling `flip_place`. Previously these could produce an empty-string key.
- The `650` handler normalizes via the shared `clean_subject` helper. In practice this gives the same result as before, because `tidy_subject` already removes the trailing dot.

