I've made the changes in the three lane files. Nothing was run, so this is untested. Matching now runs in priority order: OL key, then remote_ids, then name/date. A new author keeps its remote_ids. `build_author_reply` needed no change, because the new-author dict now carries `remote_ids` into the saved record.

Two behaviours to be aware of:
- Remote_ids added to an existing matched author are set on the in-memory record only. Nothing persists them, because existing authors are not re-saved by `build_author_reply`. Persisting them would need a change there; I did not make it.
- Conflicts raise on whichever author is finally chosen, including name/date matches, as the spec reads. A name/date match with a conflicting identifier will therefore raise rather than fall through to creating a new author.

